# A block with a round crown (an arc of radius 20) and a bore of radius 10 along it, drilled down
# (radius 4) from a plane tangent to the crown's top, up to the bore's surface: the cut fails as
# NotClosed (an edge on too many faces). Starting the drill 1 above the crown, it builds. Restated
# in round numbers from a CADFS part (00308391) that fails the same way.
sketch side(on: xz) {
  l0 = line((-30, 0), (30, 0))
  l1 = line((30, 0), (30, 20))
  l2 = line((30, 20), (20, 20))
  a3 = arc(center: (0, 20), from: (20, 20), to: (-20, 20))
  l4 = line((-20, 20), (-30, 20))
  l5 = line((-30, 20), (-30, 0))
  bore = circle((0, 20), 10)
}
body = extrude(side, 30)
sketch top(on: offset(xy, 40)) {
  c = circle((0, -15), 4)
}
drill = cut(top, upto(body.side(side.bore)))
